## Database

- **Engine:** PostgreSQL 16, SSL required (`sslmode=require`)
- **DB name:** `convision`
- **App user:** `convision_app`
- **Password:** stored in `aws_cred.txt` (never commit this file)
- **Migrations path:** `convision-api-golang/db/migrations/platform/`
- **Run migrations** (from EC2, since RDS is in private subnet):

```bash
# 1. Copy migrations to EC2
scp -r convision-api-golang/db/migrations/platform/ ec2-user@3.213.51.178:/tmp/migrations/

# 2. SSH and run
ssh ec2-user@3.213.51.178
migrate \
  -database "postgres://convision_app:<PASSWORD>@convision-dev-db.czrlj7pszo4t.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:5432/convision?sslmode=require" \
  -path /tmp/migrations/platform \
  up
```

> **IMPORTANT:** `golang-migrate` must be installed on EC2 first:
> `curl -sL https://github.com/golang-migrate/migrate/releases/download/v4.17.1/migrate.linux-arm64.tar.gz | tar xz -C /tmp && sudo mv /tmp/migrate /usr/local/bin/migrate`

> **IMPORTANT:** `AutoMigrate` (GORM) only runs when `APP_ENV=local`. For a **fresh production DB**, run the container once with `APP_ENV=local` to create all tables, then restart with `APP_ENV=production`. The SQL migrations in `db/migrations/platform/` are **patches on top of** the AutoMigrate base schema — they assume the base tables already exist.

