## Backend API on EC2

The API runs as a Docker container named `convision-api`.

### SSH access

```bash
ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa ec2-user@3.213.51.178
```

### Container management

```bash
# Check status
docker ps -a
docker logs convision-api --tail 30

# Restart with correct env (reference — use deploy.sh instead)
docker rm -f convision-api
docker run -d \
  --name convision-api \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  -p 127.0.0.1:8001:8001 \
  -e APP_ENV=production \
  -e APP_PORT=8001 \
  -e DB_HOST=convision-dev-db.czrlj7pszo4t.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com \
  -e DB_PORT=5432 \
  -e DB_DATABASE=convision \
  -e DB_USERNAME=convision_app \
  -e DB_PASSWORD=<from aws_cred.txt> \
  -e DB_SSLMODE=require \
  -e JWT_SECRET=<from aws_cred.txt> \
  -e JWT_TTL_HOURS=24 \
  -e LOG_LEVEL=info \
  -e AWS_REGION=us-east-1 \
  -e UPLOADS_BUCKET=convision-dev-uploads \
  -e BOOTSTRAP_DEFAULT_USERS=false \
  649629927448.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/convision/api:latest
```

### nginx on EC2

Config: `/etc/nginx/conf.d/convision.conf`

Listens on port 80 (redirect to HTTPS) and 443 (SSL proxy to `127.0.0.1:8001`).

```bash
sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

### BOOTSTRAP_DEFAULT_USERS

**En producción debe ser `false`.** `deploy.sh` usa por defecto `false` (sobreescribible con `BOOTSTRAP_DEFAULT_USERS=true` solo en entornos desechables).

Si se pone `true`, la API crea en el arranque (si faltan) estos usuarios demo:

| Email | Password | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `admin@convision.com` | `password` | admin |
| `specialist@convision.com` | `password` | specialist |
| `receptionist@convision.com` | `password` | receptionist |
| `laboratory@convision.com` | `password` | laboratory |

It also creates a "Sede Principal" branch if no branches exist.

