## Deployment Scripts

### `deploy.sh` — Deploy backend and/or frontend

```bash
# Deploy both (backend Docker image + frontend S3+CloudFront)
bash deploy.sh dev

# The script:
# 1. Gets EC2 IP by tag "convision-dev-api" (instance must be running)
# 2. Builds Docker image (linux/arm64) and pushes to ECR
# 3. SSHs to EC2, pulls new image, restarts container
# 4. Builds React frontend with VITE_API_URL=https://api.opticaconvision.com
# 5. Syncs dist/ to S3 convision-dev-frontend
# 6. Invalidates CloudFront cache
```

**Requires:** AWS SSO session active (`aws sso login --profile convision-admin`), Docker running locally, SSH key at `~/.ssh/id_rsa` or `~/.ssh/convision`.

### `infra.sh` — Start/stop/status infrastructure

```bash
bash infra.sh dev start    # Start EC2 + RDS
bash infra.sh dev stop     # Stop EC2 + RDS
bash infra.sh dev status   # Show current state and IPs
```

