## Terraform

```bash
cd terraform/
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply

# SSO credentials must be active first:
aws sso login --profile convision-admin
export AWS_PROFILE=convision-admin
```

Modules: `networking`, `compute`, `database`, `storage`, `cdn`, `scheduler`.

Key variables in `terraform/terraform.tfvars`:
- `root_domain = "opticaconvision.com"`
- `db_password` and `jwt_secret` — from `aws_cred.txt`
- `bootstrap_default_users = "false"` (recomendado en entorno real)

> After changing `user_data` in compute module, `terraform apply` only takes effect on new EC2 instances. For running instances, use `deploy.sh` which patches the container directly.

