## Known Issues & Fixes Applied

### `userCols` must use `password_hash` not `password`

In `convision-api-golang/internal/platform/storage/postgres/user_repository.go`:

```go
// CORRECT — matches the GORM column tag `gorm:"column:password_hash"`
const userCols = "id, name, last_name, email, identification, phone, password_hash, role, active, created_at, updated_at"
```

Using `"password"` causes login to always fail (bcrypt compare gets empty string).

### Fresh DB bootstrap order

1. Run container with `APP_ENV=local` → AutoMigrate creates all tables
2. Run SQL migrations: `migrate ... up` (skips already-applied via `schema_migrations` table)
3. Restart container with `APP_ENV=production` + `BOOTSTRAP_DEFAULT_USERS=true`

### `dev_users.go` creates default branch

`EnsureLocalDevUsers` automatically creates "Sede Principal" (branch_id=1) if no branches exist before seeding users. This prevents the FK violation on `user_branches`.

